IMPORT prelude

-- Gambling Duties Act 2022 (Singapore) -- what is a taxable gambling undertaking (ss 3, 5), what revenue duty is worked out on
-- (s 6), who pays (s 7), the time limits on assessment, objection, appeal, short levies and refunds (ss 8-11, 19), penalty tax
-- for late payment (ss 13, 14), priority in insolvency (s 18), the return and record offences and their penalties (ss 27-30),
-- and the ceiling on composition (s 37).
--
-- Edition: the deposit is the Act as enacted (No. 1 of 2022), labelled by SSO "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026", as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/GDA2022.txt. The only amendment annotation seen in the body is [Act 14 of 2022 wef 29/07/2022]
-- (in s 43, confidentiality). It is not a Revised Edition.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the duty, liability, time limits,
-- penalty tax and offences. Not encoded: the RATES and the dutiable revenue themselves (both are "prescribed" in Regulations,
-- which were not retrieved), assessment to best judgment (s 9(1)-(4)), agents for recovery (s 20), powers of entry and
-- information (ss 25, 26), administration (ss 31-36), corporate and partnership liability (ss 38, 39), confidentiality (s 43),
-- and the amendments to other Acts and transitional provisions (ss 46-52).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Gambling Duties Act 2022 -- duties`

§§ `3 and 5 -- taxable gambling undertakings`

-- s 3(6): a person conducts betting operations if the person "(a) receives bets; (b) pays, negotiates or settles bets; or (c)
-- operates a betting exchange". (9): "However, a person does not conduct betting operations ... merely because the person (a)
-- provides, or operates facilities for network access; or (b) provides services relating to ... the transmission or routing of
-- data".
GIVEN `receives bets` IS A BOOLEAN, `pays, negotiates or settles bets` IS A BOOLEAN, `operates a betting exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person conducts betting operations` IF
    `receives bets` OR `pays, negotiates or settles bets` OR `operates a betting exchange`

-- s 5(1): a gambling duty is charged on (a) betting in the course of betting operations by an AUTHORISED betting operator; (b) a
-- lottery promoted by an AUTHORISED lottery promoter; (c) keeping gaming machines, in the course of a relevant business, in
-- NON-CASINO premises; (d) a gaming service by an authorised person in the course of a relevant business -- in each case "and
-- that is prescribed". (2): subject to remission (s 12) and exemption (s 44).
-- ss 3(5), 4(4) and 2(1) ("authorised person") each EXCLUDE a casino licence holder for what the casino licence covers;
-- "non-casino premises" are premises not covered by a casino licence.
DECLARE Undertaking IS ONE OF
    `betting with an authorised betting operator`
    `a lottery by an authorised lottery promoter`
    `gaming machines in a club`
    `an online gaming service by an authorised person`
    `casino gaming under a casino licence`
    `unlicensed betting`

GIVEN `the undertaking` IS A Undertaking
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the undertaking is of a dutiable kind` IF
    CONSIDER `the undertaking`
    WHEN `casino gaming under a casino licence` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `unlicensed betting` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the undertaking` IS A Undertaking, `prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the undertaking is a taxable gambling undertaking` IF
    `the undertaking is of a dutiable kind` `the undertaking` AND `prescribed` AND (NOT `exempted`)

§§ `6 -- the revenue duty is worked out on`

-- s 6(1): duty is payable on revenue received or derived from the undertaking "and (b) is prescribed in Regulations"; (2) the
-- amount is worked out by applying the PRESCRIBED rate. (4): "any amount of goods and services tax charged ... must be
-- disregarded". (5): "No gambling duty is payable on revenue from any gaming machine the use or keeping of which is in
-- contravention of any written law."
-- The rate is an input here: none is stated in the Act.
GIVEN `revenue including GST` IS A NUMBER, `GST charged` IS A NUMBER, `from an unlawful gaming machine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the revenue duty is worked out on` MEANS
    IF `from an unlawful gaming machine` THEN 0 ELSE `revenue including GST` MINUS `GST charged`

GIVEN `revenue including GST` IS A NUMBER, `GST charged` IS A NUMBER, `from an unlawful gaming machine` IS A BOOLEAN, `prescribed rate in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the gambling duty` MEANS
    `the revenue duty is worked out on` `revenue including GST` `GST charged` `from an unlawful gaming machine` TIMES `prescribed rate in percent` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `7 -- who is liable`

-- s 7(1)-(4): duty on betting is payable by the authorised betting operator; on a lottery by the authorised lottery promoter; on
-- gaming machines by the person licensed (or exempt) to keep them at those premises "regardless that the person may not be the
-- proprietor of those premises"; on a gaming service by the authorised person. (5): two or more liable persons are jointly and
-- severally liable.
GIVEN `licensed to keep machines at the premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempt from the licensing requirement` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the proprietor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liable for the gaming machine duty` IF
    `licensed to keep machines at the premises` OR `exempt from the licensing requirement`

-- s 7(6): liability "continues until the gambling duty which is due and payable ... is and remains unpaid, despite the person"
-- ceasing to be authorised or ceasing to keep machines. (8): this section also applies to penalty tax.
GIVEN `the duty remains unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN, `has ceased to be authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is still liable` IF `the duty remains unpaid`

§§ `8 to 11 and 19 -- time limits`

-- s 8(3): additional duty under a liability notice is due "at the end of 15 days after the liability notice ... is given", or
-- at the end of an extension under (4).
GIVEN `days since the liability notice` IS A NUMBER, `extended to day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the additional duty is overdue` IF
    `days since the liability notice` GREATER THAN 15 AND `days since the liability notice` GREATER THAN `extended to day`

-- s 9(5): an assessment or reassessment "must not be made more than 5 years after the end of that period". (6): not where, in
-- the Commissioner's opinion, "fraud or wilful default has been committed" -- then "at any time".
GIVEN `years since the end of the period` IS A NUMBER, `fraud or wilful default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an assessment may still be made` IF
    `fraud or wilful default` OR `years since the end of the period` AT MOST 5

-- s 10(2)(b): a notice of objection must be made "no later than 14 days after the liability notice ... was given".
-- (4): an aggrieved objector may "within 30 days after being notified of that decision, appeal ... to the Minister".
-- (6): "The Minister's decision on an appeal is final." (8): the appeal does not suspend the liability notice.
GIVEN `days after the liability notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the objection is in time` IF `days after the liability notice` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `days after the Commissioner's decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal to the Minister is in time` IF `days after the Commissioner's decision` AT MOST 30

-- s 11(2): a demand for a short levy or erroneous refund is valid if (a) in writing; (b) by or on behalf of the Commissioner;
-- (c) "made within 5 years after the date of payment"; (d) specifies the amount or the circumstances. (3): (c) does not apply
-- where the short levy "was the result of fraud or evasion". (1): payable "within 15 days after receiving that valid demand".
GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN, `years since the payment` IS A NUMBER, `fraud or evasion` IS A BOOLEAN, `specifies the amount or circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the demand is valid` IF
        `in writing`
    AND `by the Commissioner`
    AND `specifies the amount or circumstances`
    AND (`fraud or evasion` OR `years since the payment` AT MOST 5)

-- s 11(4): "Where the short levy or erroneous refund does not exceed $200 or such other lower amount as may be prescribed ...
-- the Commissioner may waive the recovery". The $200 figure is used; a lower prescribed figure would override it.
GIVEN `the short levy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `recovery may be waived` IF `the short levy` AT MOST 200

-- s 19(1): an overpayment must be refunded "as soon as practicable"; (2) the refund "must be claimed in writing and made to the
-- Commissioner within 5 years starting the date of the overpayment".
GIVEN `claimed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `years since the overpayment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refund claim is in time` IF
    `claimed in writing` AND `years since the overpayment` LESS THAN 5

§§ `13 and 14 -- penalty tax`

-- s 13: duty not paid "before the end of the time prescribed by section 8 or 11" attracts penalty tax. s 14(1): (a) 5% of the
-- duty not paid; (b) if unpaid one month after that time, (i) "a further 5%" and (ii) "a further 5% ... for every complete month
-- thereafter". (2): "However, the total additional penalty tax must not exceed 50% of the amount of gambling duty outstanding."
-- READING: the 50% ceiling is applied to the whole penalty tax (the 5% included). The text could be read as capping only the
-- further amounts (a 55% total). See NOTES.
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS IF `x` LESS THAN `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the late-payment rate` MEANS
    IF `months` LESS THAN 1
    THEN 5
    ELSE `the smaller of` (10 PLUS 5 TIMES (`months` MINUS 1)) 50

GIVEN `paid late` IS A BOOLEAN, `complete months late` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty tax rate in percent` MEANS
    IF `paid late` THEN `the late-payment rate` `complete months late` ELSE 0

GIVEN `duty unpaid` IS A NUMBER, `paid late` IS A BOOLEAN, `complete months late` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty tax` MEANS
    `duty unpaid` TIMES `the penalty tax rate in percent` `paid late` `complete months late` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `18 -- priority in insolvency`

-- s 18(1), (2): duty or penalty tax due at the date of the bankruptcy or winding up order "and having become due within 12
-- months before" that date (for a company, before commencement of the winding up) ranks among the priority debts.
GIVEN `months before the order it became due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty ranks in priority` IF `months before the order it became due` AT MOST 12

§§ `27 to 30 -- offences`

-- s 27(1): a taxable person required to lodge a return who "intentionally or negligently fails to lodge" it in time (as extended
-- under s 21(4)) is guilty of an offence; (3) fine up to $5,000. s 21(3): the obligation continues after the time passes.
GIVEN `required to lodge a return` IS A BOOLEAN, `lodged within time or extension` IS A BOOLEAN, `intentionally or negligently` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to lodge is an offence` IF
    `required to lodge a return` AND (NOT `lodged within time or extension`) AND `intentionally or negligently`

-- s 29(1): giving a required document or information that is false or misleading in a material particular, knowing, or when the
-- person "ought reasonably to know", or reckless. (2): "it is a defence for the accused to prove, on a balance of probabilities,
-- that (a) the person does not possess the document or information required; and (b) the person has taken all reasonable steps".
GIVEN `provided required information` IS A BOOLEAN, `false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew, ought to have known or was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved non-possession` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `giving false information is an offence` IF
        `provided required information`
    AND `false or misleading in a material particular`
    AND `knew, ought to have known or was reckless`
    AND (NOT (`proved non-possession` AND `proved all reasonable steps`))

-- s 30(3): once a false statement or entry in a return or records is proved, the person "is presumed, until the contrary is
-- proved, to have made that false statement or entry with intent to evade".
GIVEN `false entry proved` IS A BOOLEAN, `contrary proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `intent to evade is presumed` IF `false entry proved` AND (NOT `contrary proved`)

-- Penalties.
-- s 27(3): fine up to $5,000 (anyone).
-- s 28(3): misleading return or records -- a special fine "and" (a) individual: $5,000 or 2 years or both; (b) otherwise: $10,000.
--   (4): the special fine is "2 times the amount of the gambling duty which has been underpaid".
-- s 29(1), (3), (4): individual $5,000 or 12 months or both; otherwise $10,000.
-- s 30(1): evasion -- a special fine "and" (d) individual $12,500 or 5 years or both; (e) otherwise $25,000. (2): special fine is
--   "4 times" the duty underpaid.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `late return or records`
    `misleading return`
    `false information`
    `evasion`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum ordinary fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `late return or records` THEN 5000
    WHEN `evasion` THEN IF `is an individual` THEN 12500 ELSE 25000
    OTHERWISE IF `is an individual` THEN 5000 ELSE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF NOT `is an individual` THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the offence`
         WHEN `late return or records` THEN 0
         WHEN `misleading return` THEN 24
         WHEN `false information` THEN 12
         WHEN `evasion` THEN 60

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `duty underpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the special fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misleading return` THEN 2 TIMES `duty underpaid`
    WHEN `evasion` THEN 4 TIMES `duty underpaid`
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `37 -- composition`

-- s 37(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of (a) one half of the amount of
-- the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000."
GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound` MEANS
    `the smaller of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
